Rename the detected Windows entry from "Windows Boot Manager" to "Windows".

Visor hardcodes the display name of the Windows entry in both the cold-scan
and hotplug paths. The firmware/BCD name is still "Windows Boot Manager", but
the boot menu only needs a short label.

--- a/src/config/config_discover.c
+++ b/src/config/config_discover.c
@@ -378,7 +378,7 @@
         if (!windows_found) {
             for (int i = 0; windows_paths[i] != NULL; i++) {
                 if (efi_file_exists_root(root, windows_paths[i])) {
-                    CHAR16 *entry_name = efi_strdup(L"Windows Boot Manager");
+                    CHAR16 *entry_name = efi_strdup(L"Windows");
                     CHAR16 *entry_icon = icon_path_for(L"windows.png");
                     CHAR16 *entry_path = efi_strdup(windows_paths[i]);
                     if (!entry_name || !entry_path) {
